88/INTERNET1 aUnited States.bGovernment Publishing Office.bLibrary Technical Services,eauthor.10aSuperintendent of Documents classification guidelines (Archived version)10aSuperintendent of Documents classification guidelines.1 aSuDocs classification guidelines1 aClassification guidelines  a[Archived version]. 1aWashington, DC :bFederal Depository Library Program,c2017- 2a[Washington, D.C.] :bGovernment Publishing Office,c2018-  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan in: 2017.  a"The current SuDocs Classification Guidelines will be published online only. Each section will include the date published and date last updated for reference ... [The] online version remains the most current and authoritative source for classification policies"--Introduction to the classification guidelines  aThe content is made available by the U.S. Government Publishing Office in accordance with Title 44 of the US Code.  aDigital collection: Federal Depository Library Program Web Archive.  a"The Superintendent of Documents Classification Guidelines were developed by staff in the U.S. Government Publishing Office (GPO), Library Services and Content Management (LSCM), Library Technical Services section with assistance from staff throughout LSCM. These guidelines are a revision of the 1993 GPO Classification Manual. The ongoing maintenance and revision of the Superintendent of Documents Classification Guidelines are the responsibility of the Cataloging Policy and Documentation Committee, Superintendent of Documents Classification Subcommittee. The Subcommittee operates within LSCM's Library Technical Services section. GPO uses the Superintendent of Documents (SuDocs) classification system to classify Federal Government publications. The SuDocs Classification Guidelines describe how to apply that system to classify and organize Federal Government publications. The purpose of these guidelines is to convey the current policies for assigning SuDocs classification numbers"--Introduction to the classification guidelines  aMode of access: Internet from the Internet Archive Wayback Machine web site. Address as of 12/4/24: https://wayback.archive-it.org/7830/*/https://www.fdlp.gov/cataloging-guidelines ; current access available via PURL.0 aArchived web page captured Sep 17, 2018 (page last updated August 14 2018); title from resource home page (viewed October 17, 2018).10aUnited States.bSuperintendent of DocumentsvHandbooks, manuals, etc. 0aClassificationxGovernment publicationszUnited StatesvHandbooks, manuals, etc.17aUnited States.bSuperintendent of Documents2fast0(OCoLC)fst00548317 7aClassificationxGovernment publications2fast0(OCoLC)fst00863664 7aUnited States2fast1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJtxgQXMWqmjMjjwXRHgrq0(OCoLC)fst01204155 0aGovernment publications 2aHandbook0(DNLM)D020479 4aOnline resources. 7ahandbooks.2aat0(CStmoGRI)aatgf300311807 7aHandbooks and manuals2fast0(OCoLC)fst01423877 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft 7aGuides et manuels.2rvmgf0(CaQQLa)RVMGF-0000010651 aUnited States.bGovernment Publishing Office,edistributor.2 aFederal Depository Library Program,ecollector.1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39QH7JmqrGyx9JWBwphj7GxvR0 tFederal Depository Library Program Web Archivew(OCoLC)88385693208iCurrent version:aUnited States. Government Publishing Office. Library Technical Services.tSuperintendent of Documents classification guidelinesw(DLC) 2018230209w(OCoLC)1057362989403Sep 17, 2018-Dec 1, 2021uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo110233zHome page by archived dates403May 15, 2022-uhttps://purl.fdlp.gov/GPO/gpo257629zHome page by archived dates4 uhttps://www.fdlp.gov/classification-guidelineszURL at time of capture4 uhttps://www.fdlp.gov/cataloging-and-classification/classification-guidelineszURL at time of capture  aC0bGPO  abc81 20181018b20181