|||||sr |||||||||||190816c20169999vaunnnngo      t  n eng c  a2019231361  a(OCoLC)1112365190  aGPObengerdacGPOdDLCdOCLCFdOCLCQdGPO  apcc  an-us---  aGPOO  a0306-B-07 (online)0 aD 1.147:00a"Voices from DARPA" podcast /cDefense Advanced Research Projects Agency.1 aVoices from Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency podcast 1aArlington, VA :bDefense Advanced Research Projects Agency,c2016-  a1 online resource (audio files) :bdigital  aIrregular  aspoken wordbspw2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan with: Ep 1 (Sept. 23, 2016).  aAvailable as streaming audio.  aListeners can subscribe and listen using podcast applications or browsers, including: Blubrry (podcast host), YouTube, and iTunes.  a"DARPA's podcast series, "Voices from DARPA," offers a revealing and informative window on the minds of the Agency's program managers. In each episode, a program manager from one of DARPA's six technical offices--Biological Technologies, Defense Sciences, Information Innovation, Microsystems Technology, Strategic Technology, and Tactical Technology--Will discuss in informal and personal terms why they are at DARPA and what they are up to. The goal of "Voices from DARPA" is to share with listeners some of the institutional know-how, vision, process, and history that together make the "secret sauce" DARPA has been adding to the Nation's innovation ecosystem for nearly 60 years"--Home page.0 aEp 1 (Sept. 23, 2016); title from serial homepage caption (DARPA, viewed on Aug. 16, 2019).1 aEp 95 (July 9, 2026) (viewed July 28, 2026).10aUnited States.bDefense Advanced Research Projects AgencyxOfficials and employeesvInterviews. 0aTechnological innovationszUnited StatesvPopular works.17aUnited States.bDefense Advanced Research Projects Agency.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00529318 7aEmployees.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00909111 7aTechnological innovations.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01145002 7aUnited State